1488	/*
1489	 * Ownership of the data buffer with freeData=true: the memory must be freeable with
1490	 * free(). On success the archive owns it and releases it exactly once, whether the
1491	 * changes are committed, overwritten again or discarded; on failure the caller keeps
1492	 * the ownership and may free it immediately. freeData=false leaves the ownership to
1493	 * the caller in every case. Run under valgrind/ASAN (see the Makefile tests targets):
1494	 * a regression surfaces as a double-free, invalid free or leak here.
1495	 */
